# Docker build context for the API image.
#
# This matters more than it looks. Without it the context is ~937 MB, of which ~930 MB is
# `apps/web/node_modules` and `apps/web/.next` — the frontend build, which the API image never
# touches. The API itself is under 1 MB. Every Render build re-uploads the whole context, so on
# a free tier this is the difference between a build that finishes and one that times out.
#
# Rule of thumb: the API needs core/, modules/, apps/api/, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml and
# data/fetch.sh. Everything else is excluded below.

# --- frontend: the entire Next.js tree ----------------------------------------
apps/web/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/.turbo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- version control -----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- python caches and tooling -------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/

# --- data: fetched at build time by data/fetch.sh, never shipped in the context
data/raw/
data/*.csv

# --- local environment: must never be baked into an image ----------------------
# Secrets belong in the platform's env var store, not in a layer that anyone who can pull the
# image can read.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- CI, docs, deploy metadata -------------------------------------------------
.github/
docs/
deploy/
render.yaml
README.md
LICENCE
LICENSE

# --- OS / editor ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
